      <description>&lt;!--&#xA;How to use hugo:&#xA;open VSCode &amp; type cd WillR_Portfolio to pput the terminal&#xA;in that folder. you may need to do cd C:\ then cd Hugo/WillR_Portfolio&#xA;&#xA;Then, make edits to the markdown files in the content folder&#xA;then use hugo server -D to post the server with the draft pages included&#xA;&#xA;Ctrl + C to stop the server, Ctrl + S to reload (if any changes were made)&#xA;&#xA;STILL NEED TO FIGURE OUT:&#xA;use &#34;hugo new posts/[folder]/index.md&#34; to add a new page in a new folder&#xA;i.e. hugo new posts/RPS/index.md&#xA;&#xA;**BEFORE I ADD ANY OF THESE:&#xA;I SHOULD GO INTO CONFIG.TOML AND ADD DEFAULT AUTHOR / AVATAR / other things&#xA;https://hugo-theme-dream.g1en.site/params-configurations#:~:text=author%20%3D%20%22g1eny0ung,%E4%B8%8D%E5%A6%82%E9%A9%AC%E4%B8%8A%E5%87%BA%E5%8F%91%E3%80%82%22&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;C:\Hugo\WillR_Portfolio\themes\hugo-theme-dream-master\config.toml&#xA;that&#39;s to edit params and stuff&#xA;&#xA;hugo new posts/Alarmclock/index.md&#xA;hugo new posts/PC/index.md&#xA;hugo new posts/Battery_Charger/index.md&#xA;hugo new posts/Plasma_Cutter/index.md&#xA;hugo new posts/LF3DP/index.md&#xA;hugo new posts/Photography/index.md&#xA;hugo new posts/A4988/index.md&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;then put images in the folder (this is called a branch)&#xA;&#xA;Use # to create a heading (regular markdown stuff), this will separate &#xA;the preview section of the page from everything else&#xA;&#xA;https://g1en.site/categories/&#xA;https://github.com/g1eny0ung/blog/blob/master/data/socials.toml&#xA;https://hugo-theme-dream.g1en.site/summary-images&#xA;https://www.markdownguide.org/cheat-sheet/&#xA;&#xA;https://azleslie.com/projects/hugo-tutorial/&#xA;&#xA;add lots more content&#xA;&#xA;HOW TO DEPLOY STUFF TO THE SITE (updating)&#xA;&#xA;make changes (to the files in Documents &gt; Hugofiles &gt; WillR-Portfolio &gt; content)&#xA;&#xA;save all&#xA;&#xA;make a backup somewhere &#xA;&#xA;open CMD as cd ..administrator &#xA;&#xA;cd into C:/Users/wmroh/Documents/Hugofiles/WillR-Portfolio &#xA;use &#39;cd ..&#39; to go back one level if needed&#xA;&#xA;do&#xA;deploy.sh &#34;[insert commit message]&#34; (just a comment)&#xA;&#xA;OR&#xA;&#xA;do the following commands in order:&#xA;hugo --cleanDestinationDir&#xA;robocopy public thewamr.github.io /MIR /XD .git&#xA;cd thewamr.github.io&#xA;git add .&#xA;git commit -m &#34;your message&#34;&#xA;git push origin main&#xA;&#xA;make sure &#xA;# &lt;a href=&#34;/&#34;&gt;Back to Home Page&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;is on the top and bottom of every page for navigation. I wish there was a better way, but this will do (until im not burnt out of github anymore)&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Also, about images. for some reason, some images are processed as &#34;[name].JPG&#34; instead of &#34;[name].jpg&#34;. This capitalization screws with everything. IT&#39;S SO STUPID. if you notice broken images, don&#39;t bother changing the file extension manually, just go into the markdown file and change the image call to the capital JPG. &#xA;&#xA;it&#39;s dumb but that&#39;s how it works.&#xA;&#xA;also also&#xA;putting&#xA;&#xA;[markup.goldmark.renderer]&#xA;unsafe = true&#xA;&#xA;in hugo.toml may solve the issues with putting raw html in there&#xA;(can&#39;t remember if it&#39;s true or false, idk)&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span style=&#34;color: maroon;&#34;&gt;Color&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color: white;&#34;&gt;Test!&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;Tags:&#xA;- Skills/tools: PCB Design · Altium · KiCAD · SolidWorks · Ansys · Femap · FEA · Topology Optimization · CAD · CNC Machining · Plasma Cutting · 3D Printing · Sheet Metal · Aluminum Extrusion · Soldering · Hand Assembly&#xA;- Topics: Microcontroller · Bare-Metal · ATmega32U4 · ESP32 · Arduino · USB-C · I2C · Stepper Motors · Shift Register · Battery Management · Power Electronics · Mixed-Signal · Binder Jet · Autoclave · CoreXY · Structures · Balsa · Aerodynamics&#xA;- Context: JLCPCB · Texas A&amp;M · SAE Aero · RPS · Lab Project · Personal Project · Documentation&#xA;- Status: Complete · In Progress · Shelved · Handed Off&#xA;&#xA;Categories:&#xA;- Electronics&#xA;- Mechanical&#xA;- Aerospace&#xA;- Shop&#xA;&#xA;--&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Howdy! I&amp;rsquo;m Will, a mechanical engineering student at Texas A&amp;amp;M. I also spend a lot of my time on electronics and embedded systems, plus anything else where I get to design something from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This site is a portfolio and a logbook. Projects are ordered with the most substantial work at the top. Click through any of them for the full story.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
